1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,880
You know about the Black Panther Party, but what about the White Panther Party?

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,540
Founded in 1968 by poet and rock band manager John Sinclair,

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:12,340
the White Panther Party was created to support the Black Panther Party

4
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:16,480
and fight white supremacy, capitalism, and state violence.

5
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,540
And yes, they were white.

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,560
But they weren't trying to lead, though.

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,580
They followed the leadership of black revolutionaries.

8
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:28,760
The White Panther Party is now the Panther Party, and I am a member of that party.

9
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,760
You can go join them, too, at thepantherparty.com.

10
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:33,900
And no, it's not just for white people.

11
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:36,660
We got rid of the white part and just named it the Panther Party.

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,960
We work in tandem with the Black Panther Party.

13
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,600
We do not separate from each other.

14
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,620
We support each other, and we see each other as comrades, not allies.

15
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:46,120
Go check out the bpp.us.

16
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:47,920
That is the new Black Panther website.

17
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:53,200
We are about to roll out some very aggressive, revolutionary organizing

18
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,780
for communities and community survivals.

19
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,740
Some plans to organize communities across the nation

20
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,720
and form solidarity with all kinds of movements.

21
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:05,880
The Brown Berets, the Palestine movement, the American Indian movement,

22
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,420
the Rednecks, the veterans, the patriots, all that good stuff.

23
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:10,680
We're coming back.

24
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,280
All of us are coming back.

25
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,120
It's like the 1960s all over again.

26
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,460
As always, love you, fam.

27
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:45,380
Thank you so much.

